@node Cpatch
@chapter Cpatch: Runtime C Hot-Patching

@cindex cpatch
@cindex hot-patch
@cindex defun swap

@quotation
This chapter mirrors @file{doc_org/cmacs/cpatch.org}.
@end quotation

@code{cpatch} is the kernel-grade companion to cintrospect.  Where
cintrospect lets you @emph{inspect} the running C layer, cpatch lets
you @emph{replace} C functions in place at runtime --- the C-side
equivalent of redefining a Lisp function with @code{defun}.

This is @emph{off by default} and lives in its own subsystem
@file{cmacs/cpatch/} for a reason: a wrong patch silently corrupts
in-process state.  Enable with @option{--enable-cmacs-cpatch}; the
flag requires @option{--with-cmacs-cintrospect}.

@section Two patching modes

@table @asis
@item DEFUN pointer swap (Phase 1, available now)
Atomic write to @code{Lisp_Subr.function} in
@file{src/lisp.h:2175-2208}.  Safe because Emacs Lisp eval is
single-threaded.  Covers all ~2,400 Lisp-callable C primitives.

@item Trampoline detour (Phase 3, deferred)
13-byte @code{mov rax,imm64; jmp rax} on x86_64 / 12-byte
@code{adrp/add/br x16} on AArch64, with mprotect W^X dance, ICache
flush, libopcodes prologue probe, and rendezvous with cmacs's
quiescence flags.  In Phase 1, @code{cmacs-c-patch-function} signals
@code{cmacs-cpatch-not-implemented}.
@end table

@section Lisp DEFUNs

@table @code
@item cmacs-c-patch-defun SYM NEW-FN-ADDR
Atomically swap @code{Lisp_Subr.function} for the DEFUN named SYM.
Records the original pointer for later restore.

@item cmacs-c-unpatch-defun SYM
Restore the original pointer for a single DEFUN.

@item cmacs-c-patch-list
Return list of currently-applied patches with original/patched
addresses.

@item cmacs-c-unpatch-all
Panic button.  Restores every patched DEFUN.  Returns the count.

@item cmacs-c-patch-function NAME ADDR
@itemx cmacs-c-unpatch-function NAME
@itemx cmacs-c-patch-diff SYM SOURCE
Phase-3 stubs.
@end table

@section MCP gating

When @option{--with-cmacs-mcp} is also enabled, MCP-driven patching
remains @emph{off} until the user opts in:

@example
(setq cmacs-mcp-cintrospect-enable-patching t)
@end example

The @code{M-x} user trusting their own commands is @emph{not} the
same trust level as a remote MCP client.

