@node Build Configuration
@chapter Build Configuration

@section Configure Flags

CMacs features are auto-detected at configure time.  For a
fully-featured build matching Fedora defaults, use:

@example
./configure \
  --with-pgtk \
  --with-cairo \
  --with-dbus \
  --with-harfbuzz \
  --with-modules \
  --with-native-compilation=aot \
  --with-tree-sitter \
  --with-sqlite3 \
  --with-json \
  --with-rsvg \
  --with-jpeg \
  --with-png \
  --with-gif \
  --with-tiff \
  --with-webp \
  --with-xpm \
  --with-gpm=no \
  --with-cmacs-glib \
  --with-cmacs-gi \
  --with-cmacs-crispy \
  --with-cmacs-bacon \
  --with-cmacs-gowl \
  --with-cmacs-podomation \
  --with-cmacs-libreclaw \
  --with-cmacs-org-ex \
  --with-cmacs-mcp \
  --with-cmacs-print \
  --with-cmacs-cintrospect \
  --enable-cmacs-cpatch
@end example

@noindent
To install somewhere other than @file{/usr/local}, pass
@option{--prefix} at configure time.  For example, to install under
@file{~/.local}:

@example
./configure --prefix=$HOME/.local \
  ...                              # same flags as above
make -j$(nproc)
make install                       # no sudo needed for ~/.local
@end example

@noindent
@code{--with-cmacs-bacon} builds libbacon statically from
@file{deps/bacon/} and links it into the CMacs binary.  For distro
packaging, use @code{--with-cmacs-bacon=system} to link against a
system-installed @code{bacon-1.0} via pkg-config instead.

