@section Building the Bacon Module

The @command{cmacsgi} module is compiled into the CMacs binary by
default (via the bundled libbacon static link).  For standalone or
development use, it can also be built as a loadable @file{.so}:

@example
cd cmacs/bacon/modules/
make
@end example

This produces @file{cmacs_gi.so} for use with an external
@command{bacon} binary.

@section Compile Flags

The Emacs build system picks up CMacs objects via @code{configure.ac}:

@example
CMACS_GLIB_OBJ="cmacs-glib-loop.o cmacs-gobject.o
                 cmacs-gclosure.o cmacs-dbus-service.o
                 cmacs-eval-dispatch.o"
CMACS_GI_OBJ="cmacs-gi.o"
CMACS_CRISPY_OBJ="cmacs-crispy.o"
CMACS_BACON_OBJ="cmacs-bacon.o cmacs-bacon-ipc.o"
@end example

C source files live under @file{cmacs/} and are symlinked into
@file{src/} for the build system.

@section Building on Ubuntu 24.04 / older hosts

Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (noble) --- and other distributions that have not
yet caught up with the wlroots 0.19 release cadence --- ship
versions of several gowl dependencies that are too old to satisfy
@code{pkg-config --exists wlroots-0.19}.  Noble specifically ships
wlroots 0.17, wayland 1.22, wayland-protocols 1.34, and pixman
0.42, while gowl requires wlroots @geq{}0.19, wayland
@geq{}1.23.1, wayland-protocols @geq{}1.38, and pixman
@geq{}0.43.  @code{libdex-dev} is also absent from the noble
archive entirely.

Because gowl's @file{config.mk} queries all required pkg-config
modules in a single invocation, a single missing package causes
@code{pkg-config --cflags} to return an empty string, which then
cascades into a @code{fatal error: glib.h: No such file or
directory} when the vendored @file{yaml-glib} sources are
compiled.  The real fix is to satisfy the version gates, not to
patch the include paths.

First install everything apt @emph{can} provide, including the
mcp and podomation runtime deps:

@example
sudo apt install \
  meson ninja-build pkg-config \
  libglib2.0-dev libjson-glib-dev libsoup-3.0-dev libetpan-dev \
  libdrm-dev libxkbcommon-dev libudev-dev libinput-dev \
  libseat-dev libdisplay-info-dev libliftoff-dev hwdata \
  libgbm-dev libvulkan-dev glslang-tools \
  libxcb1-dev libxcb-composite0-dev libxcb-ewmh-dev \
  libxcb-icccm4-dev libxcb-render-util0-dev libxcb-res0-dev \
  libxcb-xinput-dev
@end example

Then build the out-of-date components into @file{/usr/local}, in
dependency order: wayland 1.23.1, wayland-protocols 1.38, pixman
0.44, libdex 0.9.1, and finally wlroots 0.19.  Each uses the
standard meson recipe, e.g.@:

@example
git clone -b 0.19 https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots.git
cd wlroots
meson setup build --prefix=/usr/local
ninja -C build && sudo ninja -C build install
sudo ldconfig
@end example

See @file{doc_org/cmacs/build.org} for the full step-by-step
recipe including every intermediate dependency.

Everything installs under @file{/usr/local}, which is @emph{not}
on Ubuntu's default pkg-config search path.  Export
@code{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} in every shell where you run
@command{./configure} or @command{make} for cmacs:

@example
export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/usr/local/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/pkgconfig:/usr/local/lib/pkgconfig
pkg-config --modversion wlroots-0.19   # => 0.19.x
pkg-config --modversion libdex-1       # => 0.9.x
@end example

If a gowl compile fails with @code{glib.h: No such file or
directory} despite glib being installed, run
@code{pkg-config --print-errors --exists} on the full
@code{DEPS_REQUIRED} list from @file{deps/gowl/config.mk} to
identify the missing module.  Do not try to patch the include
paths directly --- the empty @code{CFLAGS_DEPS} is a symptom of
an unmet version gate somewhere in the list.

@bye
